# Root-anchored: `go build ./cmd/orchestrator` (the README/CI build step) drops a
# bare `orchestrator` binary in the repo root. Anchored with a leading slash so
# it never shadows the tracked cmd/orchestrator/ package directory.
/orchestrator
.last_run_id

# RFC 0048 Phase 1 (D2): the web-console embed dir holds only the committed
# placeholder index.html in git. PR 3's `make ui` writes the real Svelte/Vite
# bundle (hashed JS/CSS, .vite/, etc.) into internal/ui/assets/ — build
# artifacts that must never be committed. These rules live here, not in a
# co-located internal/ui/assets/.gitignore, so the `//go:embed all:assets` tree
# embeds only web assets and never serves a VCS file at /ui/.gitignore.
#
# Caveat: index.html below is the one tracked path the build also OVERWRITES
# (Vite emits its own index.html referencing the hashed bundle). So after
# `make ui` the working tree shows index.html as modified — that diff is build
# output and must NOT be committed: a committed build-output index.html points
# at gitignored hashes that are absent on a clean checkout, 404-ing every asset
# and erasing the placeholder. The `go` CI lane guards this by asserting the
# checked-in index.html is still the placeholder. After a local `make ui`, run
# `git checkout -- internal/ui/assets/index.html` to restore it.
internal/ui/assets/*
!internal/ui/assets/index.html

# RFC 0048 Phase 1 PR 3: the web/ frontend toolchain. node_modules/ is covered
# by the global rule above; these catch the Vite caches and any stray local
# build output (`make ui` writes the bundle into internal/ui/assets/, ignored
# above — not into web/). Only web/ source + the committed lockfile are tracked.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
